# canary: the only wrong TRUE the corpus ever produced (#51). BMC explored an
# impossible branch after an undecided feasibility check, found every path
# below it contradictory, explored nothing, and still discharged 62 obligations
# -- including an unconditional out-of-bounds read -- as exhaustively proven.
# Expected FALSE; UNKNOWN is honest and scores as unproven, TRUE means the
# completeness claim has come back.
sv-comp/argv-tasks/Pan_exceptionprone.yml no-runtime-exception

# canaries: the seeded-precondition guard let the BMC treat a call as
# non-throwing because its preconditions were emitted as obligations -- while
# under valid-assert those obligations are not consumed at all, so nothing
# carried the burden. Eight wrong TRUEs. The flag that says whether they are
# seeded was computed for a decision record and never stored, so it sat at its
# default for every property.
sv-comp/securibench/Basic29.yml valid-assert
sv-comp/securibench/Basic30.yml valid-assert
sv-comp/securibench/Datastructures5.yml valid-assert
sv-comp/securibench/Factories3.yml valid-assert
sv-comp/securibench/Inter4.yml valid-assert

# CHC: an obligation inside a catch needs exceptional edges in BOTH encoders
sv-comp/jbmc-regression/ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException1.yml valid-assert
sv-comp/jbmc-regression/ClassCastException1.yml valid-assert

# CHC: uninterpreted space invariants can be read as empty (vacuous proof)
sv-comp/MinePump/spec1-5_product45.yml valid-assert
sv-comp/java-ranger-regression/TCAS_prop1.yml valid-assert

# #48: the bitvector BMC proved `1.0f + 1.0e-8f > 1.0f` because `bvadd` on the
# two IEEE-754 bit patterns exceeds the first, while the JVM's `fadd` returns
# exactly 1.0f. A confirmed wrong TRUE, caught only because float-search found
# the violation and replay certified it.
ajave/jvm-floats/FloatIsNotDouble.yml valid-assert

# Engine seams: an interval hint published at a join must hold on both paths.
# Without the join fix, smt-bmc discharges the assertion and Blackboard::contested
# reports a JVM-confirmed contradiction (2026-10-27).
ajave/engine-cooperation/IntervalHintAtAJoinMustHoldOnBothPaths.yml valid-assert

# Heap: the site-indexed field refinement, and the escape rule it rests on.
ajave/heap/TwoObjectsDistinctFieldValues.yml valid-assert
ajave/heap/UnknownReceiverReadsTheMergedCell.yml valid-assert

# B3: array element values, and the rule that a store at an index the domain
# cannot evaluate must weaken every element (2026-10-27).
ajave/heap/ArrayElementWrittenThenRead.yml valid-assert
ajave/heap/ArrayStoreAtUnknownIndexWeakensEveryElement.yml valid-assert

# C1: a heap effect crossing a call through the summary relation, and the frame
# condition that keeps a non-writing callee from invalidating anything (2026-10-27).
ajave/engine-chc/FieldWrittenInACalleeIsVisibleToTheCaller.yml valid-assert
ajave/engine-chc/ACalleeThatWritesNothingInvalidatesNothing.yml valid-assert

# The CHC encoders read arrays they never wrote: a reused local slot made the
# store's receiver ambiguous and havoced every array. Constant bound, so no
# quantified invariant is involved (2026-10-27).
ajave/heap/ArrayElementNonNullWithAConstantBound.yml valid-assert

# D1's beneficiary: a universally quantified array invariant inferred from one
# loop and consumed in another. UNKNOWN without AJAVE_CHC_QGEN, TRUE with it —
# the only task in this set that prices that flag (2026-10-27).
ajave/heap/EveryElementNonNullAfterAFillLoop.yml valid-assert

# C1's confirmed soundness defect (#106). FALSE by construction, JVM-validated.
# With AJAVE_CHC_HEAP_SUMMARY=1 and the falsifiers disabled, CHC answers TRUE.
# Canary so the fix is demonstrated and the defect cannot silently return.
ajave/engine-chc/RecursiveFieldWriteIsNotForgotten.yml valid-assert

# #108: a failing check forks control into its exception handler, so an
# assertion reachable only through an implicitly-thrown exception stops being
# unreachable to the BMC. The trio separates three mechanisms that all look
# alike -- explicit throw, implicit-and-deterministic, implicit-and-input-
# dependent -- and only the last one needed the fix (2026-10-29).
ajave/jvm-exceptions/AssertionReachedOnlyByAnImplicitThrow.yml valid-assert
ajave/jvm-exceptions/ImplicitThrowReachesItsHandlerOnlyForSomeInputs.yml valid-assert

# The boundary of what quantified generalisation reaches, as a pair. The
# fill-loop benchmark above is TRUE with AJAVE_CHC_QGEN and UNKNOWN without.
# This one needs the same kind of fact -- forall n . value[n] >= 0 -- but
# established by a *guard* in one method and consumed by a *traversal* in
# another, and qgen does not find it. UNKNOWN is the honest answer today;
# a TRUE here is a real capability gain and should be celebrated, not
# suppressed (2026-10-29).
ajave/heap/NegativeIsNeverFoundBecauseOnlyNonNegativeIsStored.yml valid-assert

# The relational-bounds gap, in six lines. UNKNOWN by design today: the
# interval domain is `BTreeMap<VarId, Interval>` and cannot express
# `i < a.length`, which is the entire content of the proof. A TRUE here means
# a weakly relational domain landed, and is a real capability gain
# (gh #119, 2026-10-30).
ajave/jvm-arrays/FillLoopOfUnboundedLengthStaysInBounds.yml no-runtime-exception
# The copy-chain half of the same gap. `a[j] = a[j] + 1` reaches the store
# three copies removed from the index the guard constrained, so a relational
# domain that does not transfer facts across `x = y` loses them before the
# obligation. Bytecode-specific, not domain-specific (gh #119, 2026-10-30).
ajave/jvm-arrays/NestedFillLoopRelatesBothIndicesToTheLength.yml no-runtime-exception
# The non-strict guard shape, 24% of the budget population. `i <= n-1` needs
# two relations composed -- `i <= t` and `t < n` -- because `i <= len` alone is
# false exactly at the off-by-one (gh #119, 2026-10-30).
ajave/jvm-arrays/NonStrictGuardBoundsTheIndexJustAsWell.yml no-runtime-exception
# The flattened-matrix lemma: `a[i*s + j]` against `new T[m*s]`, which is
# non-linear and beyond Pentagons, difference bounds and Octagons alike. Both
# halves of the obligation need it -- the abstract interval for the index
# overflows, so even `idx >= 0` is otherwise unprovable (gh #119, 2026-10-31).
ajave/jvm-arrays/FlattenedMatrixIndexStaysInBounds.yml no-runtime-exception

# Pentagons reduction: a relation must tighten the interval, not only answer
# comparisons. The second is deliberately unproven -- it names the one fact
# (a parameter's upper bound crossing a call) that is still missing.
ajave/jvm-arrays/OuterCounterKeepsItsLowerBoundAcrossAnInnerLoop.yml valid-assert
ajave/jvm-arrays/FlattenedMatrixIndexAcrossACall.yml no-runtime-exception

# gh #88: a call declared "modelled" but encoded as a free variable. The hash
# of a literal is a constant, and the BMC used to claim it could be anything.
ajave/jvm-strings/LiteralStringHashIsAConstantNotAFreeVariable.yml valid-assert

# Large-block encoding (gh #128). The first is the minimal program: 24
# one-armed ifs, which the old reachability join declined on every one and so
# forked, exhausting MAX_FORKS. The second pins the Alarm family, 893 blocks in
# one Simulink-generated method, which went from 0 to 36 points across both
# properties -- it is the task that shows the path-length bound was capping the
# size of method the engine could traverse at all, not its effort.
ajave/engine-bmc/AChainOfOneArmedIfsMustNotForkPerBranch.yml valid-assert
sv-comp/java-ranger-regression/alarm/Alarm_prop2.yml valid-assert
# The FALSE twin. Merging is new discharge surface, and the TRUE twin cannot
# tell a correct merge from one that silently loses an arm -- losing an arm
# still leaves the invariant holding. Here the lost arm is the one carrying the
# violation, so the same bug reads as a wrong TRUE at -32.
ajave/engine-bmc/AMergedRegionMustNotLoseTheArmThatBreaksTheInvariant.yml valid-assert

# gh #130: an invariant proved in LIA must not prune a bitvector search.
# Synthesis published a map that was inductive over unbounded integers, the
# hint path handed it to the BMC, and the BMC pruned the throwing path while
# still claiming all_paths_complete -- a wrong TRUE at -32. The first is the
# corpus task it fired on; the second is the minimal program.
sv-comp/algorithms/BellmanFord-FunUnsat01.yml no-runtime-exception
ajave/engine-ai/ALiaProvedBoundMustNotPruneABitvectorSearch.yml no-runtime-exception
